WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.707
The CrestApps Tenant Hierarchy lets one tenant create and run its own child

00:00:05.707 --> 00:00:09.774
tenants, and lets its people open them without signing in again.

00:00:09.774 --> 00:00:14.423
This video shows the problem it solves, how it is organized, every screen,

00:00:14.423 --> 00:00:16.980
and how it keeps each tenant isolated.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:26.342
Many organizations run a separate site for each customer they serve:

00:00:26.342 --> 00:00:30.911
a bookkeeping firm keeps one per client, an agency one per brand.

00:00:30.911 --> 00:00:36.510
With plain multi-tenancy, only the platform administrator can create those sites.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:41.926
The organization's staff then need a separate account and password on every customer

00:00:41.926 --> 00:00:45.970
site, and nothing ties what they do there back to the person who did it.

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:50.926
And the more sites one team manages, the more a single mistake could

00:00:50.926 --> 00:00:53.540
let one customer's site reach another's.

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:58.332
The Tenant Hierarchy makes such an organization a parent.

00:00:58.332 --> 00:01:03.272
It creates and runs its own child tenants, its people open them without

00:01:03.272 --> 00:01:06.480
a password, and every tenant stays isolated.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:12.904
The main site is the platform.

00:01:12.904 --> 00:01:18.650
Its administrator decides which tenants become parents, and sets a policy for each one.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:25.114
A parent creates, edits, suspends and removes its own child tenants, within that

00:01:25.114 --> 00:01:29.100
policy, and decides which of its people may open them.

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:34.902
Each child tenant is a complete site, with its own address, users and data.

00:01:34.902 --> 00:01:40.390
People from the parent arrive signed in, with only the roles the parent gave them.

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:45.270
Every action is recorded in the parent's audit trail, so you can always

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:48.220
tell who did what, where, and how they signed in.

00:01:52.406 --> 00:01:58.440
On the platform, Multi-Tenancy, Tenant Hierarchy lists every parent with its child tenants,

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:01.364
the way the Tenants screen lists tenants.

00:02:01.364 --> 00:02:05.346
Riverside Accounting is already a parent, with one client.

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:08.608
Let's make Contoso Bookkeeping a parent.

00:02:08.608 --> 00:02:11.905
Click Make a Parent Tenant, and pick the tenant.

00:02:11.905 --> 00:02:17.460
Its display name and address fill in from the tenant, so its address does not change.

00:02:17.913 --> 00:02:22.701
The policy sets how many child tenants the parent may have, the setup

00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:26.659
recipes they can start from, and where their data lives:

00:02:26.659 --> 00:02:30.873
a file, a database, a schema or a table prefix for each one.

00:02:31.326 --> 00:02:36.261
It also lists the features child tenants never get, the permissions their own

00:02:36.261 --> 00:02:41.376
users never get, and how many days a removed child tenant can still be restored.

00:02:41.376 --> 00:02:43.636
Let's keep them for thirty days.

00:02:44.089 --> 00:02:51.680
Opening child tenants can require two-factor authentication, and sessions can end after a period without activity.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:56.109
The tenant switcher opens a picker page, or shows it in a panel.

00:02:56.562 --> 00:02:58.820
Finally, the words on screen.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:04.241
Contoso calls itself a practice, and calls its child tenants clients, so every

00:03:04.241 --> 00:03:07.532
screen of the parent says Client and Clients.

00:03:07.982 --> 00:03:10.165
Click Make parent tenant.

00:03:10.165 --> 00:03:14.602
Contoso Bookkeeping is now a parent, with no clients yet.

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:23.211
In the parent, Jamie, Contoso's owner, opens Clients.

00:03:23.211 --> 00:03:25.010
The list is empty.

00:03:25.464 --> 00:03:27.747
Click Add client and type the name.

00:03:27.747 --> 00:03:31.646
The address fills in from it, and the screen checks at once that

00:03:31.646 --> 00:03:33.094
the address is free.

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:38.366
Pick what the new site starts from, such as a blank site, and click Create client.

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:41.464
The client is set up in the background.

00:03:41.464 --> 00:03:46.758
The list shows Setting up, and refreshes on its own to Running, with an Open button.

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:53.669
Contoso has a few more clients now.

00:03:53.669 --> 00:03:56.520
Click Open next to Northwind Traders.

00:03:56.971 --> 00:04:00.619
Jamie lands in the client's admin, already signed in.

00:04:00.619 --> 00:04:03.402
No password was asked, and none exists:

00:04:03.402 --> 00:04:06.741
the parent vouched for her with a one-time code.

00:04:07.191 --> 00:04:09.580
The building icon shows where you are:

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:14.681
working in Northwind Traders, as a linked account of Jamie, through Contoso Bookkeeping.

00:04:15.135 --> 00:04:18.423
Switch client lists the clients Jamie may open.

00:04:18.423 --> 00:04:22.145
Mark favorites with the star, and pick another client.

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:27.389
From any client, Back to Contoso Bookkeeping returns to the parent, and Leave

00:04:27.389 --> 00:04:29.815
this client signs out of the client.

00:04:34.004 --> 00:04:38.025
Manage, next to a client, holds everything else:

00:04:38.025 --> 00:04:45.024
edit its name, address and description, its features, its access rules and its activity.

00:04:45.477 --> 00:04:48.566
Features turns features of the client on or off.

00:04:48.566 --> 00:04:53.087
Features that could reach other sites are hidden, and some are always on.

00:04:53.542 --> 00:04:58.082
Suspend closes the client to everyone, including its own staff.

00:04:58.729 --> 00:05:04.389
Its address then shows that the site is not available, never the platform or another site.

00:05:04.841 --> 00:05:06.691
Resume opens it again.

00:05:06.691 --> 00:05:10.721
To remove a suspended client, type its name to confirm.

00:05:15.273 --> 00:05:20.346
The policy keeps removed clients for thirty days, so the client waits, removal

00:05:20.346 --> 00:05:23.003
scheduled, and Restore brings it back.

00:05:27.204 --> 00:05:29.530
Clients, Access holds the rules.

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:34.059
Each one says who in Contoso may open which clients, and which roles

00:05:34.059 --> 00:05:36.324
they have once they are inside.

00:05:36.776 --> 00:05:41.639
The parent's administrators can open every client, as administrators.

00:05:41.639 --> 00:05:46.956
Let's let everyone with the Bookkeeper role open every client, as an editor.

00:05:47.409 --> 00:05:49.804
A rule can also name one person.

00:05:49.804 --> 00:05:53.649
Rules on a client's own page apply to that client only.

00:05:54.101 --> 00:05:58.651
Someone who matches several rules gets all of their roles, and someone who

00:05:58.651 --> 00:06:01.039
matches none cannot open the client.

00:06:01.039 --> 00:06:05.191
Removing a rule ends the sessions that depend on it within minutes.

00:06:09.391 --> 00:06:15.220
Clients, Activity opens the audit trail, filtered to the tenant hierarchy:

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:21.631
every client created, opened, suspended or removed, and every access rule changed.

00:06:22.085 --> 00:06:25.762
Each event says who did it and when, with the client, the roles

00:06:25.762 --> 00:06:29.385
someone received, how they signed in, and the network address.

00:06:29.837 --> 00:06:31.991
Details shows the whole event.

00:06:31.991 --> 00:06:36.537
Events can be turned off and trimmed like any other audit trail event.

00:06:40.721 --> 00:06:45.824
Back on the platform, the hierarchy shows both firms and their clients.

00:06:45.824 --> 00:06:48.211
Each parent sees only its own.

00:06:48.663 --> 00:06:54.203
Search finds a parent by its name or address, or by those of its clients.

00:06:54.656 --> 00:06:56.459
Manage opens a parent:

00:06:56.459 --> 00:07:01.161
suspend or resume it with all its clients, move a client to another

00:07:01.161 --> 00:07:03.416
parent, or remove everything.

00:07:07.616 --> 00:07:13.008
Opening a client follows the shape of the OAuth authorization code flow with PKCE.

00:07:13.008 --> 00:07:17.910
The one-time code is random, lives sixty seconds, works once, and only for

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:21.036
the client and the browser that asked for it.

00:07:21.786 --> 00:07:25.469
In the client, people from the parent are linked accounts.

00:07:25.469 --> 00:07:29.901
They have no password, nobody can edit them there, and their roles come

00:07:29.901 --> 00:07:31.916
only from the parent's rules.

00:07:32.666 --> 00:07:34.528
Guards keep tenants apart:

00:07:34.528 --> 00:07:39.593
code in one tenant cannot reach another outside the broker, blocked features stay

00:07:39.593 --> 00:07:44.426
hidden, and outbound requests cannot reach other tenants or private networks.

00:07:45.176 --> 00:07:49.771
Cookies stay on each tenant's own address, a client page cannot call its

00:07:49.771 --> 00:07:54.249
parent from a script, and the address of a suspended or removed tenant

00:07:54.249 --> 00:07:56.076
never shows another site.

00:08:00.276 --> 00:08:05.360
In Program.cs, call AddTenantHierarchy inside AddOrchardCms.

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:12.756
It installs the guards in every tenant, and does nothing for a tenant outside a hierarchy.

00:08:13.506 --> 00:08:19.697
In appsettings.json, the Tenant Hierarchy section names the platform domain that parent addresses

00:08:19.697 --> 00:08:24.086
go under, and the database servers child tenants can be created on.

00:08:24.836 --> 00:08:27.856
SQL Server and PostgreSQL are built in.

00:08:27.856 --> 00:08:33.762
For another server, implement I Child Tenant Database Provisioner and register it:

00:08:33.762 --> 00:08:38.326
it creates each client's database and login, and removes them.

00:08:40.326 --> 00:08:45.046
The Tenant Hierarchy gives an organization its own sites to run for its

00:08:45.046 --> 00:08:50.441
customers, one sign-in to reach them all, and a record of everything done in them.

00:08:50.441 --> 00:08:52.036
Thanks for watching.

